# question: If a clinician is concerned about a patient's organ, which alarms would be relevant?
#
# CORRECTED after a self-audit (see cq_discoveries.md's "audit correction"
# entry) -- the first version only reached Organ via the DIAGNOSTIC chain
# (Metric -approximates-> Property -isPropertyOf-> Process -presentIn->
# Organ). It missed the independent THERAPEUTIC chain inference.ttl also
# declares as a class-level bridge (Device -administers-> TherapeuticModality
# -targetsProcess-> Process -presentIn-> Organ, fired from the device's
# TYPE alone, no Metric needed) -- and, on the strength of that omission,
# I originally told you organ:Kidneys was "empirically dead in this corpus"
# because mda:administers is never ASSERTED in kg_generated.ttl. That was
# wrong: it's ENTAILED, for every archetype on one of five device classes
# (Dialysator, ExtracorporealMembraneOxygenator, Incubator, Thermoregulator,
# MechanicalVentilator -- see inference.ttl's Technical axioms section),
# with or without a Metric.
#
# Corrected result: organ:Kidneys now appears (1 alarm -- "PRISMAFLEX -
# Algemene systeemfout", a Dialysator archetype with no Metric at all,
# reached purely via administers/RenalReplacementTherapy/RenalFiltration/
# presentIn), and organ:Lungs grows from 20 to 31 alarms -- every ventilator
# connectivity/technical fault (e.g. "SERVOU - Volume uit blokkade",
# "TRILOGY - 0x79") is organ-relevant via device capability even with zero
# measurement content. organ:BloodVessels (5) and organ:Heart (3) are
# genuinely unaffected -- no administers-bridged device targets either.
#
# reasoning: required
#
# Known incomplete, still: of the 15 distinct metrics, 3 don't reach an
# organ via the diagnostic chain -- metric:Pulse (no approximates bridge
# at all), metric:Humidity and metric:AirTemperature (dead-end one and two
# hops short of an organ respectively) -- see cq_discoveries.md. None of
# their devices (PhysiologicalMonitor) carry an administers bridge either,
# so this correction does not rescue them.

PREFIX mda: <https://w3id.org/mda/ontology#>

SELECT ?organ (GROUP_CONCAT(DISTINCT ?label; separator=" | ") AS ?alarms)
       (COUNT(DISTINCT ?a) AS ?matchCount) WHERE {
  ?a a mda:AlarmType ; mda:hasLabel ?label ; mda:hasMessage/mda:triggeredBy ?dev .
  {
    ?a mda:hasMessage/mda:triggeredBy/mda:hasFunctionalUnit/mda:hasSensor/mda:sensorProducesSignal/(mda:analyzedBy/mda:producesSignal)*/mda:analyzedBy/mda:producesMetric/mda:approximates/mda:isPropertyOf/mda:presentIn ?organ .
  } UNION {
    ?dev mda:administers/mda:targetsProcess/mda:presentIn ?organ .
  }
}
GROUP BY ?organ
ORDER BY ?organ
